":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What condition is required for applying linearity of expectation?","options":["The relevant expectations are finite","The variables are independent","The variables are normal","The variables have the same distribution"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b261518830092719bee52b5b"},{"id":"pt_batch8_linearity_of_expectation_004","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Unlike $E[X+Y]=E[X]+E[Y]$, the identity $\\operatorname{Var}(X+Y)=\\operatorname{Var}(X)+\\operatorname{Var}(Y)$ requires:","options":["$X,Y$ uncorrelated (e.g. independent)","nothing more than finite variances","$X=Y$, the identical variable","$E[X]=E[Y]$, i.e. equal means"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9586fca0a4b3e08cf1c38dc8"},{"id":"pt_batch8_linearity_of_expectation_005","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Writing a count as $X=I_1+\\cdots+I_n$ to find $E[X]$ works because:","options":["$E[I_i]=1$ for every indicator","$E[X]=\\sum E[I_i]$ even if dependent","the indicators must be independent","each indicator has variance $0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"75fdfc4be4c0df43f9d2f3cf"},{"id":"pt_batch8_linearity_of_expectation_006","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $E[X]=2$ and $E[Y]=5$, what is $E[X+Y]$?","options":["$7$","$10$","$3$","$25$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"98dda9ca595140b3183b1f68"},{"id":"pt_batch8_linearity_of_expectation_007","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $E[X]=3$, what is $E[4X]$?","options":["$7$","$3/4$","$4$","$12$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0906473e38679543902a7c7e"},{"id":"pt_batch8_linearity_of_expectation_008","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $E[X]=1$ and $E[Y]=2$, what is $E[3X+4Y]$?","options":["$9$","$11$","$24$","$7$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"37bfd5d685932fb89746b8a5"},{"id":